;; expect: main.derive refused derive_shape
;; what has no derivation is refused before anything is generated — a type without constructors (the
;; header's), a proposition, Nat (the integer: the elaborator's own rows), an inductive applied to a
;; value, a name that is no type; each with its reason (define_test.sh reads the five records)
(import Init Int.decEq)
(type Void)
(derive Void eq)
(derive True eq)
(derive Nat eq)
(derive (Fin 3) eq)
(derive Nope eq)
